From u267c7c6c510dc8a2 at groups.google.com  Mon Jan 27 17:56:16 2014
From: u267c7c6c510dc8a2 at groups.google.com (Ian Fellows)
Date: Mon, 27 Jan 2014 17:56:16 +0000
Subject: Re: Two or more variables in plot
Message-ID: <xRfOeLFOudw.VfmsPLBmptkJ@deducer.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <xRfOeLFOudw.e-34pdfkPSMJ@deducer.groups.google.com>
References: <xRfOeLFOudw.e-34pdfkPSMJ@deducer.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/deducer/c/xRfOeLFOudw/m/VfmsPLBmptkJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

you will need to have your data in "long" format, with one variable representing categories, and the other the values. For example something like:

Variable    Value
cat1          .323
cat1          .33
cat2          .5
cat1          .6

you can then specify "Variable" as the x-axis and "Value" as the y-axis in a boxplot using the plot builder.

ian

